{
    "FormatVersion": 2,
    "DisplayName": "Cirrus",
    "Notes": "Ice, eight kilometres up, a quarter of a cumulus' extinction and a wispy edge cut by the finer of the two shipped noise volumes. The only type in the library that names a volume of its own, and the proof that a type's edge travels with the type. Anisotropy 8.00 IS THE POINT OF THIS FILE. Cirrus is not a field of thin blobs, it is fibrous bands combed out downwind by the shear ice falls through - and until a type carried its own placement field no profile, however authored, could turn a round patch into a band. Scale 0.60 with it, and the pair is what makes a FIBRE rather than a sheet: at the layer's 12 km tile the across-wind cell is about 1.80 km and the along-wind one about 14.4 km. Scale 2.50 was tried first and measured away - it makes each band 7.5 km across, which fills the zenith with one flat sheet and answers a different complaint than the one this file is for. SCALE 0.35 WAS ALSO MEASURED AWAY, and the reason is a coupling this file did not know it had: since the coverage field moved onto the billowy Alligator pair, the volume a type names decides its PLACEMENT CELLS as well as its edge, and CloudNoise_FineWisp halves both. At 0.35 with that volume the finest cell was 160 m, the median chord of cirrus along a view ray was 128 m against a march that searches at 234 m, and three quarters of those chords were thinner than one search step - 3.66x past Nyquist, the worst in the library, and visible as dither along every strand. 0.60 puts the finest cell at 275 m, which is what Desert/Tests/Engine/CloudType now asserts against the schedule. DETAIL FACTOR 0.625, DOWN FROM 2.50, AND IT IS A RE-BASE RATHER THAN A RE-ART-DIRECTION. The depth of the cut is the layer's Detail Strength TIMES this number, and the 2.50 was authored when that strength was 0.10 - an effective cut of 0.25. Task DS raised the layer to 0.40 because below it the cut is finer than the march can resolve, and at 0.40 the old 2.50 gives an effective cut of 1.00: measured against a cloudless frame at the same camera, this type's contribution to the picture falls from 33 per cent of its un-eroded self to 4.3 per cent. A cirrus is thin - a DENSITY factor of 0.35 and an extinction of 0.25 - so a deep cut does not shred it, it deletes it. 0.625 restores the effective 0.25 the file was authored at, exactly. What makes this type wispy is its DetailCharacter of 0 and the fine volume it names, not the depth of the cut.",
    "NoiseVolume": "Clouds/CloudNoise_FineWisp.dcnv",
